<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> I will love thee, O LORD, my strength.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> The LORD <i>is</i> my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, <i>and</i> my high tower.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> I will call upon the LORD, <i>who is worthy</i> to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> The sorrows of hell compassed me about: the snares of death prevented me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, <i>even</i> into his ears.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness <i>was</i> under his feet.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings of the wind.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>11</b></sup> He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round about him <i>were</i> dark waters <i>and</i> thick clouds of the skies.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>12</b></sup> At the brightness <i>that was</i> before him his thick clouds passed, hail <i>stones</i> and coals of fire.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>13</b></sup> The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail <i>stones</i> and coals of fire.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>14</b></sup> Yea, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>15</b></sup> Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were discovered at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>16</b></sup> He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>17</b></sup> He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them which hated me: for they were too strong for me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>18</b></sup> They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>19</b></sup> He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>20</b></sup> The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>21</b></sup> For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>22</b></sup> For all his judgments <i>were</i> before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>23</b></sup> I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>24</b></sup> Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>25</b></sup> With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>26</b></sup> With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>27</b></sup> For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>28</b></sup> For thou wilt light my candle: the LORD my God will enlighten my darkness.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>29</b></sup> For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>30</b></sup> <i>As for</i> God, his way <i>is</i> perfect: the word of the LORD is tried: he <i>is</i> a buckler to all those that trust in him.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>31</b></sup> For who <i>is</i> God save the LORD? or who <i>is</i> a rock save our God?<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>32</b></sup> <i>It is</i> God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>33</b></sup> He maketh my feet like hinds’ <i>feet</i>, and setteth me upon my high places.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>34</b></sup> He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>35</b></sup> Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>36</b></sup> Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>37</b></sup> I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>38</b></sup> I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they are fallen under my feet.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>39</b></sup> For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>40</b></sup> Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>41</b></sup> They cried, but <i>there was</i> none to save <i>them</i>: <i>even</i> unto the LORD, but he answered them not.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>42</b></sup> Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>43</b></sup> Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; <i>and</i> thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people <i>whom</i> I have not known shall serve me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>44</b></sup> As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>45</b></sup> The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid out of their close places.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>46</b></sup> The LORD liveth; and blessed <i>be</i> my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>47</b></sup> <i>It is</i> God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>48</b></sup> He delivereth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>49</b></sup> Therefore will I give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and sing praises unto thy name.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day <i>that</i> the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,</title><sup><b>50</b></sup> Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore. <br />
